        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(swarm): add QuickJS guest orchestration",
        "body": "Related: #110325\n\n<details>\n<summary>Additional instructions</summary>\n\n**MUST:** Keep **Allow edits from maintainers** enabled for this PR so maintainers\ncan help update the branch when needed.\n\n</details>\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw's landed Swarm core can launch and collect concurrent agents, but QuickJS Code Mode cannot yet orchestrate those collectors directly. Code Mode guests need a typed, gated surface that can survive snapshot parking and host restart without duplicating launches or polling collector state.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nImplements the QuickJS Code Mode Swarm surface from `docs/plan/swarms.md` §7 behind `tools.swarm`. The guest receives typed `agents.run`, `phase`, and `log` globals; agent launches use a parked host bridge with requester-scoped, restart-surviving `(codeModeRunId, bridgeId)` replay identity and request fingerprinting; lifecycle notes project through session events; and collector settlement is event-driven instead of polled.\n\nThe Gateway launch idempotency key remains a distinct globally safe identity, while the replay key is scoped and canonicalized to the requester session. No SQLite schema-version change is involved; the persisted record additions are additive.\n\n## User Impact\n\nWhen Swarm is enabled, Code Mode programs can launch collector agents, await their structured results across parked snapshots and restarts, and emit phase/log progress. The surface remains off by default with `tools.swarm` disabled, and the generated `agents.d.ts` virtual file gives Code Mode callers typed guidance.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused Vitest proof: 10 files across unit-fast, gateway, and agents shards; 265 tests passed. Final post-rebase smoke: 4 files, 117 tests passed.\n- `pnpm ui:build`: passed; 2,353 modules transformed, 532 finalized Control UI sidecars verified, startup performance within limits.\n- `pnpm plugin-sdk:surface:check`: passed; 353 entrypoints, 8,601 exports, 0 package-exported forbidden subpaths.\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports`: production, full-tree, and script scans passed with 0 unused exports.\n- `pnpm format <touched files>` and `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Fresh full-branch autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
